Bootstrap: docker
From: nvcr.io/nvidia/tensorflow:25.02-tf2-py3@sha256:c83b37d26f19ab00d8a13cf974edd079c3d099918ec3110c304a989d6e2f75d5

# Aetherscan container recipe.
#
# Compatible with both Apptainer (>=1.3) and SingularityCE (>=4.0). Build it on
# the target cluster so the resulting .sif uses that cluster's native runtime:
#
#   # Apptainer (Ampere cluster, 1.4.5):
#   apptainer build aetherscan-ngc25.02.sif aetherscan.def
#
#   # SingularityCE (Blackwell cluster, 4.1.1):
#   singularity build aetherscan-ngc25.02.sif aetherscan.def
#
# The NGC TensorFlow 25.02 base image ships TF 2.17 with Python 3.12, CUDA 12.8,
# cuDNN 9.7.1, NCCL 2.25.1, and the Blackwell-ready kernels (sm_120). NVIDIA has
# announced 25.02 as the final NGC TF container; if Aetherscan ever needs to
# migrate off it, swap the `From:` line and re-test.
#
# Host driver requirements:
#   - Blackwell cluster: driver >=570 (native CUDA 12.8 support).
#   - Ampere cluster:    driver >=550 (host CUDA 12.4) works via CUDA forward
#                        compatibility -- the NGC base ships cuda-compat-12-8,
#                        which --nv layers in so TF sees the container's CUDA
#                        12.8 stack without needing a host driver upgrade.
#                        Verified on driver 550.78 + A4000 (6 GPUs detected).

%files
    # Stage to /opt rather than /tmp: Singularity bind-mounts the host's /tmp
    # over the container's /tmp during %post (so the host's noexec/nodev
    # constraints don't break temp use), which would hide files placed in /tmp
    # by %files. /opt is part of every NGC TF base image and is stable.
    requirements-container.txt /opt/aetherscan-requirements.txt

%post
    # Install pip extras layered onto the NGC base.
    pip install --no-cache-dir -r /opt/aetherscan-requirements.txt
    rm -f /opt/aetherscan-requirements.txt

%environment
    # Prevent the container from picking up host-side Python packages, which
    # would otherwise shadow the carefully-pinned versions inside the image.
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    # Quieten TF startup noise; INFO+ still prints, only the C++ INFO floodgate closes.
    export TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL=1

%labels
    Maintainer Zach Yek <xiaoxiyek1.5@gmail.com>
    Project    Aetherscan
    Base       nvcr.io/nvidia/tensorflow:25.02-tf2-py3@sha256:c83b37d26f19ab00d8a13cf974edd079c3d099918ec3110c304a989d6e2f75d5
    Python     3.12
    TF         2.17
    CUDA       12.8
    cuDNN      9.7.1
    NCCL       2.25.1
    Purpose    Blackwell (sm_120) + Ampere (sm_86) GPU support for Aetherscan

%help
    Aetherscan runtime image (Python 3.12 / TF 2.17 / CUDA 12.8). Runs on both
    Blackwell (sm_120, driver >=570) and Ampere (sm_86, driver >=550 via CUDA
    forward compatibility) -- one recipe, both clusters.

    Use utils/run_container.sh from the repo root to launch commands, e.g.:
        ./utils/run_container.sh python -m aetherscan.main train --save-tag test
